WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.830 line:15%
I love a salmon during the holidays.

2
00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:04.380 line:15%
It's like a little unexpected.

3
00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:06.750 line:15%
So this is a really, really easy recipe.

4
00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:08.660 line:15%
You're basically gonna take your little whisk here.

5
00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:12.970 line:15%
This is some honey, some Dijon mustard,

6
00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:14.580 line:15%
a couple little spices in there.

7
00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.170
And you're just gonna mix it all up.

8
00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:17.003
I love honey.

9
00:00:17.003 --> 00:00:18.090
And what it's gonna do in the air fryer

10
00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:19.640 line:15%
is it's gonna kind of caramelize

11
00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:20.610 line:15%
and make it a little thicker

12
00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:21.730 line:15%
so it's gonna stay in place

13
00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:25.090 line:15%
versus like running off of the salmon.

14
00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:25.944 line:15%
Yes.

15
00:00:25.944 --> 00:00:26.777 line:15%
So we'll take our salmon

16
00:00:26.777 --> 00:00:28.260 line:15%
and we'll just put it right in there.

17
00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:30.410 line:15%
And it's gonna coat all over it.

18
00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:31.380
If you wanna get real crazy,

19
00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:32.520
you can leave it in like a marinade

20
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:33.973
but you really don't have to.

21
00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:38.360
The trick with the salmon is parchment paper.

22
00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:40.140
And it's one thing I really love to use

23
00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:40.973
with this recipe

24
00:00:40.973 --> 00:00:42.610
because have you ever cooked salmon

25
00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:44.830
and then the skin comes off on the pan?

26
00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:47.250 line:15%
And you're like oh, this looks like a mess.

27
00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:48.850 line:15%
The parchment paper will save your skin

28
00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:50.900 line:15%
and you'll get that beautiful like crispy skin

29
00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:51.930 line:15%
on the bottom,

30
00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:52.810 line:15%
which also makes it easier

31
00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:54.690 line:15%
when you're serving it to everybody.

32
00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:57.610
So preheating your air fryer a couple minutes.

33
00:00:57.610 --> 00:00:59.480
This is nice and warm now.

34
00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:00.940
We're gonna take it out.

35
00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:03.730
Okay, so this is gonna just lay right into the bottom,

36
00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:05.590
and then you're gonna just put your salmon on top,

37
00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:06.983
skin side down.

38
00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:11.150
And I do like to keep a little of the sauce

39
00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:13.660
on the side that has not been contaminated

40
00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:15.110
with your raw salmon.

41
00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:17.170
So afterwards, you can add some extra sauce

42
00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:19.790
if you like things a little bit saucy.

43
00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:21.130
I'm gonna put that in.

44
00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:23.300
And depending on the size of your salmon,

45
00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:24.920
like six to seven minutes.

46
00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:26.210
You don't wanna go too crazy

47
00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:27.462
'cause then it'll be really dry.

48
00:01:27.462 --> 00:01:30.045 line:15%
(upbeat music)

